SWEET WLAN kept link: Get 103 carries the join target's real IEs from the first answer (patch 0293, run wd6-rec1: Settings showed "Weak Security" on the joined WPA2-PSK network). Cause [obs-RE docs/research/W-D3-weak-security.md]: Settings snapshots the Get 103 record ONCE at link-up and never refreshes it; our record had the privacy bit and ie_len 0 until the first keep scan ended, so IO80211 marked it WEP. The L23 scan (or the WLC_GET_BSS_INFO answer of patch 0288) already reads the join target's whole record; swl25r_keep (sweet_wlan_l25_rsne.h, patch 0206) now also keeps its IE block (<= 1024 B), rates, beacon period, noise, SNR and chanspec in struct swl25_tgt. sw_keep_capture hands them to sweet_wlan_a80211_kept_target (patch 0201), which holds them until the radio is attached; swr_kept_target (sweet_wlan_radio.h) cuts the IEs to 512 B at an IE boundary with the scan record's GAP rules, and Get 103 prefers the scan-list entry of the joined BSSID if it has IEs, else this record. Never privacy-set with ie_len 0 silently: with no IEs source a GAP says Settings will show Weak Security (the privacy bit stays). Also Get 2 AUTH_TYPE answers lower 1 / upper 8 while joined with WPA2-PSK (metrics only). Not run on hardware.
